# The self type, the one primitive under all inductive types, and the bottom of
# the shared foundation with the Seed kernel. A self type binds a value to its
# own type, so its members are the terms that inhabit a family applied to
# themselves. The self combinator names the fixed point of a family. The
# universe, the type of types, is the self-type identity. Every later type, the
# booleans, the naturals, the integers, the algebra tower, is a self type whose
# body states its own induction principle. Nothing else is added as a primitive.
structure self-type
  head type
  # The family whose fixed point this self type names.
  link family, like type
  # A value belongs to the self type when it inhabits the family applied to
  # itself. This is the rule the kernel checks by normalization.
  assert self-membership
    head type, have type
    have family
